| C11 | As of the lock date, \(D_9\) is the first case beyond the authors' published verified range for which no later public resolution was located. | Inference from C04, C06, and the dated search | Supported within two recorded search passes; not globally provable from bibliographic databases | C04 restricts the family to \(n\ge4\), C06 reports all \(n\le8\), and both the pre-discovery and post-result searches in [`search_log.md`](search_log.md) found no post-2020 proof, disproof, \(D_9\) certificate, \(n\ge9\) verification, or general \(D_n\) solution. The second pass used zbMATH, OpenAlex, OpenCitations, Crossref, arXiv, focused repository searches, and current author records. A current secondary tracker also labels the conjecture open: [MathDB entry](https://mathdb.com/p/342030/normalized-flow-conjecture-for-the-absolute-order-of-type-d); this tracker is a freshness signal, not primary evidence. Access failures listed separately in the log are excluded from this inference. | Medium-high | The title “Type \(D_9\)” remains a defensible finite research boundary after the independent post-result audit. Phrase it as “first case beyond the published \(n\le8\) report,” not as an absolute priority claim over unpublished work. |
| C15 | No relevant public code repository or exact \(D_9\) certificate was found in the recorded searches. | Negative search result | No hit in two independently phrased passes; not a universal nonexistence claim | The first pass searched the DOI/arXiv ID, exact title, published verification sentence, and source terminology. The post-result pass instead searched `G(2,2,9)`, `D9`/`D_9` + `Sperner`, even signed permutations, Farkas/orbit-flow terminology, and type-\(D\) absolute-order repositories through authenticated GitHub search, Zenodo, and the accessible OSF endpoints. Focused queries returned zero relevant hits. Figshare's API returned HTTP 403 and is therefore an access limitation, not negative evidence. Full query strings and counts are in [`search_log.md`](search_log.md). | Medium-high within the searched public repositories | The contractually required independent post-result novelty search has been completed. Refresh it if release is materially delayed; retain the qualification about private or unindexed artifacts. |
